---
const { lang, t } = Astro.props;

import { languages, defaultLang, useTranslations } from '../../i18n/ui';



import { NeatBackground } from '../../components/NeatBackground';
import VsHeroLockup from '../../components/VsHeroLockup.astro';



import ClosingCta from "../ClosingCta.astro";
---

  <div class="flex flex-col isolate">
 <section class="relative isolate overflow-hidden pt-24 pb-16 sm:pt-32 sm:pb-24 lg:pt-40 lg:pb-24">
     <NeatBackground client:idle />

      
      <div class="px-4 mx-auto max-w-7xl text-center lg:px-12 relative z-10">
        <VsHeroLockup name="Hasura" logo="/img/competitors/hasura-logo-primary-darkbg.svg" logoClass="h-6 sm:h-7"/>
        <h1 class="mb-6 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl text-white">
          Rebase vs Hasura
        </h1>
        <p class="mb-10 text-lg leading-8 text-surface-300 lg:text-xl sm:px-16 xl:px-48">
          Hasura is phenomenal at generating GraphQL APIs over Postgres. But APIs alone don't solve back-office problems. See why teams prefer Rebase when they need instant Admin Panels and tight logic bundling alongside their generated REST endpoints.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <!-- Content Sections -->
 <section class="relative z-0 py-16 sm:py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 lg:px-8">
        
        <div class="space-y-16">
          
          <!-- Point 1 -->
          <div class="py-2">
              <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center justify-between gap-4 mb-8">
                <div>
                  <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-primary/30 bg-primary/10 text-primary text-sm font-medium mb-3">
                    
<svg
  class="lucide lucide-circle"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="2"
  stroke-linecap="round"
  stroke-linejoin="round"
>
  <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" />
</svg>

                    The Frontend Gap
                  </div>
                  <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white">Missing Admin Interfaces</h3>
                </div>
              </div>
              
              <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 relative">
                <!-- VS Badge -->
                <div class="hidden md:flex absolute left-1/2 top-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 w-10 h-10 rounded-full border border-surface-700 bg-surface-900 items-center justify-center text-xs font-semibold text-surface-400 z-10 shadow-xl">VS</div>
                
                <!-- Competitor Card -->
                <div class="bg-surface-800/20 rounded-xl p-6 border border-surface-700/50 relative overflow-hidden">
                  <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-32 h-32 bg-red-500/5 blur-[50px] -mr-16 -mt-16"></div>
                  <div class="relative">
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
                      
<svg
  class="lucide lucide-circle-alert"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="2"
  stroke-linecap="round"
  stroke-linejoin="round"
>
  <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" />
  <line x1="12" x2="12" y1="8" y2="12" />
  <line x1="12" x2="12.01" y1="16" y2="16" />
</svg>

                      <h4 class="text-white font-semibold">The Hasura Pain</h4>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-surface-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Hasura purely focuses on the API layer. While it creates GraphQL instantly, it gives nothing to your non-technical teammates. To manage the data going through those APIs, you still have to build an admin panel from scratch or cobble it together with Retool.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Rebase Card -->
                <div class="bg-primary/5 rounded-xl p-6 border border-primary/20 relative overflow-hidden">
                  <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-32 h-32 bg-primary/10 blur-[50px] -mr-16 -mt-16"></div>
                  <div class="relative">
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
                      
<svg
  class="lucide lucide-circle-check-big"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="2"
  stroke-linecap="round"
  stroke-linejoin="round"
>
  <path d="M21.801 10A10 10 0 1 1 17 3.335" />
  <path d="m9 11 3 3L22 4" />
</svg>

                      <h4 class="text-white font-semibold">How Rebase Solves This</h4>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-surface-300 leading-relaxed text-sm mb-4">
                      Rebase generates both the API layer AND the application layer.
                    </p>
                    <ul class="text-surface-400 space-y-3 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
<svg
  class="lucide lucide-check"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="2"
  stroke-linecap="round"
  stroke-linejoin="round"
>
  <path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5" />
</svg>
 <span class="leading-relaxed">Rebase generates real REST APIs based on your Postgres Schema.</span></li>
                  <li class="flex items-start">
<svg
  class="lucide lucide-check"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="2"
  stroke-linecap="round"
  stroke-linejoin="round"
>
  <path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5" />
</svg>
 <span class="leading-relaxed">Rebase ALSO generates a gorgeous, React-based Admin tool with out-of-the-box editing, auditing, and dashboards.</span></li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Point 2 -->
          <div class="py-2">
              <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center justify-between gap-4 mb-8">
                <div>
                  <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-primary/30 bg-primary/10 text-primary text-sm font-medium mb-3">
                    
<svg
  class="lucide lucide-git-branch"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="2"
  stroke-linecap="round"
  stroke-linejoin="round"
>
  <path d="M15 6a9 9 0 0 0-9 9V3" />
  <circle cx="18" cy="6" r="3" />
  <circle cx="6" cy="18" r="3" />
</svg>

                    Business Logic Complexity
                  </div>
                  <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white">Fragmented Logic Networks</h3>
                </div>
              </div>
              
              <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 relative">
                <!-- VS Badge -->
                <div class="hidden md:flex absolute left-1/2 top-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 w-10 h-10 rounded-full border border-surface-700 bg-surface-900 items-center justify-center text-xs font-semibold text-surface-400 z-10 shadow-xl">VS</div>
                
                <!-- Competitor Card -->
                <div class="bg-surface-800/20 rounded-xl p-6 border border-surface-700/50 relative overflow-hidden">
                  <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-32 h-32 bg-red-500/5 blur-[50px] -mr-16 -mt-16"></div>
                  <div class="relative">
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
                      
<svg
  class="lucide lucide-circle-alert"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="2"
  stroke-linecap="round"
  stroke-linejoin="round"
>
  <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" />
  <line x1="12" x2="12" y1="8" y2="12" />
  <line x1="12" x2="12.01" y1="16" y2="16" />
</svg>

                      <h4 class="text-white font-semibold">The Hasura Pain</h4>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-surface-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">When you need to run business logic in Hasura (e.g. charging a Stripe customer when a row is inserted), you have to set up "Actions" or "Event Triggers"—which requires you to stand up, deploy, and maintain an entirely separate server backend to receive webhooks.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Rebase Card -->
                <div class="bg-primary/5 rounded-xl p-6 border border-primary/20 relative overflow-hidden">
                  <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-32 h-32 bg-primary/10 blur-[50px] -mr-16 -mt-16"></div>
                  <div class="relative">
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
                      
<svg
  class="lucide lucide-circle-check-big"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="2"
  stroke-linecap="round"
  stroke-linejoin="round"
>
  <path d="M21.801 10A10 10 0 1 1 17 3.335" />
  <path d="m9 11 3 3L22 4" />
</svg>

                      <h4 class="text-white font-semibold">How Rebase Solves This</h4>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-surface-300 leading-relaxed text-sm mb-4">
                      Rebase is a unified Node.js backend environment.
                    </p>
                    <ul class="text-surface-400 space-y-3 text-sm">
                      <li class="flex items-start">
<svg
  class="lucide lucide-check"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="2"
  stroke-linecap="round"
  stroke-linejoin="round"
>
  <path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5" />
</svg>
 <span class="leading-relaxed">Your custom business logic runs in the exact same Node process as your generated endpoints.</span></li>
                  <li class="flex items-start">
<svg
  class="lucide lucide-check"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="2"
  stroke-linecap="round"
  stroke-linejoin="round"
>
  <path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5" />
</svg>
 <span class="leading-relaxed">No network hop latency for internal triggers, no disjointed webhook configurations.</span></li>
                  <li class="flex items-start">
<svg
  class="lucide lucide-check"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="2"
  stroke-linecap="round"
  stroke-linejoin="round"
>
  <path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5" />
</svg>
 <span class="leading-relaxed">Maintain everything elegantly in one TypeScript repository.</span></li>
                    </ul>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
          </div>

          
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Neat gradient divider -->
    <div class="neat-divider relative -my-72 pointer-events-none overflow-hidden" style="z-index: -1; height: 600px;">
        <NeatBackground variant="a" client:visible/>
    </div>


    <!-- CTA Section -->
 <section class="py-16 sm:py-24 border-t border-surface-800/40">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl mb-6">Experience the unified backend.</h2>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-x-6">
          <a href="/docs" class="inline-flex items-center gap-x-2 rounded-lg bg-primary px-6 py-3 text-base font-semibold text-white hover:bg-primary-dark hover:brightness-105 transition-all duration-200 ease-in-out btn-glow">
            Get Started
            
<svg
  class="lucide lucide-arrow-right"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="2"
  stroke-linecap="round"
  stroke-linejoin="round"
>
  <path d="M5 12h14" />
  <path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7" />
</svg>

          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <!-- Back to the comparison hub -->
    <section id="compare-hub-footer" class="py-16 sm:py-20 border-t border-surface-800/60">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
        <p class="mb-4 text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.25em] text-primary/80 uppercase">Keep comparing</p>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white mb-4">
          Not the comparison you needed?
        </h2>
        <p class="text-base text-surface-400 mb-8 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
          The hub explains the four kinds of tool Rebase gets confused with, the five questions that actually
          differ, and the cases where you should pick something else.
        </p>
        <a href="/compare"
           class="inline-flex items-center gap-x-2 rounded-lg bg-primary px-6 py-3 text-base font-semibold text-white hover:bg-primary-dark hover:brightness-105 transition-all btn-glow mb-8">
          All comparisons
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
               stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M5 12h14"/>
            <path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/>
          </svg>
        </a>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2">
                    <a href="/rebase-vs-supabase" class="text-sm text-surface-400 hover:text-primary transition-colors">vs Supabase</a>
                    <a href="/rebase-vs-firebase" class="text-sm text-surface-400 hover:text-primary transition-colors">vs Firebase</a>
                    <a href="/rebase-vs-directus" class="text-sm text-surface-400 hover:text-primary transition-colors">vs Directus</a>
                    <a href="/rebase-vs-strapi" class="text-sm text-surface-400 hover:text-primary transition-colors">vs Strapi</a>
                    <a href="/rebase-vs-payload" class="text-sm text-surface-400 hover:text-primary transition-colors">vs Payload</a>
                    <a href="/rebase-vs-retool" class="text-sm text-surface-400 hover:text-primary transition-colors">vs Retool</a>
                    <a href="/rebase-vs-django" class="text-sm text-surface-400 hover:text-primary transition-colors">vs Django</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  
    <ClosingCta title="Don't take our word for it." blurb="The comparison that matters is the one you run. Point Rebase at a Postgres database you already have and see how it holds up next to Hasura." trackId="vs-hasura" />

</div>
